    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“You make sure people walk away instead of carried.”</em></p><p>When you take point on a mission, negotiation, or defense, you’re listening for the moment things could stop breaking.</p><ul><li>When a <strong>scene or encounter you lead</strong> (as face, tactical commander, or moral center) ends with <strong>zero fatalities</strong> on either side—surrender, withdrawal, incapacitation, or mutual stand-downs all count—your faction may gain <strong>+1 Unity/Victory Point</strong> for the current or next strategic turn.</li><li>This can happen at most <strong>once per scene</strong>, and the GM should only award it when your presence and choices clearly guided things away from bloodshed.</li></ul>",
